       Filename entries can be read from a directory stream using rreeaaddddiirr(3).

       The  underlying file descriptor of the directory stream can be obtained
       using ddiirrffdd(3).

       The ooppeennddiirr()  function  sets  the  close‐on‐exec  flag  for  the  file
       descriptor  underlying  the _D_I_R _*.  The ffddooppeennddiirr() function leaves the
       setting of the close‐on‐exec flag unchanged for  the  file  descriptor,
       _f_d.   POSIX.1‐200x  leaves  it unspecified whether a successful call to
       ffddooppeennddiirr() will set the close‐on‐exec flag for  the  file  descriptor,
       _f_d.

